{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions","id":757625,"title":"No beast specific crafted items? (and other odd questions)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-05T18:32:47-08:00","id":757625,"title":"No beast specific crafted items? (and other odd questions)","content":"I noticed there was a distinct lack of items that beast can craft that are specific to their splat... did I miss something or is that intentional? (can they use the gear of other supers?)<br /> <br /> Also.. I cant recall what the beast aura/blood effects was supposed to be for crossover purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T19:18:10-08:00","id":757741,"title":"","content":"I am reasonably certain that a Beast's aura reflects the nature of their Horror. <br /> What do you mean by blood effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T19:35:41-08:00","id":757754,"title":"","content":"If one of the Kindred gets anything special for drinking their blood. If I remember correctly, 1e had some specific rules for what each splat's blood meant in terms of Vitae for a Kindred. Promethean blood was stale and gave half Vitae, Uratha blood was especially nourishing and gave a penalty to resist Frenzy, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T19:51:35-08:00","id":757774,"title":"","content":"Aaah. No idea there, though I suspect any Kindred who drank a Beast's blood would have some very strange nightmares when next they slumbered. Or did whatever it is that kindred do when the sun is up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T20:52:06-08:00","id":757844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions#post757625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed there was a distinct lack of items that beast can craft that are specific to their splat... did I miss something or is that intentional? (can they use the gear of other supers?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast magic is fairly basic and built on fundamentals, whereas item crafting tends to be among the most involved/refined/complicated types of supernatural power that exists \u2014 consider, for contrast's sake, that Demon gives the Unchained gadget-creation as an innate ability. Generally speaking, if a Beast has magic items at their disposal, they're either stolen or gifted to them.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, consider also that Mother's Kiss can be applied to item-crafting magic just as readily as any other powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also.. I cant recall what the beast aura/blood effects was supposed to be for crossover purposes. </div> </div> </div>The general trajectory of aura-reading powers in second edition seems to be moving towards a more abstracted and personalized set of signifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T04:12:45-08:00","id":758391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions#post757625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed there was a distinct lack of items that beast can craft that are specific to their splat... did I miss something or is that intentional? (can they use the gear of other supers?)</div> </div> </div> </div> No items. Its not the only game with the lack of items (vampire doesn't either) so its probably intentional. Its simply not thematic for them to have magic items, so it probably didn't come up. <i>Heroes</i> using magic items to slay monsters is thematic (and they kinda do get the magic item, but in the form of hero-powers). Monsters using magic items to slay heroes isn't. There's no reason for there to be magic tiems in BtP. <br /> <br /> It makes sense for mages to enchant items. Prometheans and demons are built around alchemical/technological aspects, plus the whole holy themes in those games, so it makes sense. Fae use enchanted items in stories all the time. Geist kinda has enchanted items, but their Memento are generally glorified equipment bonuses instead of something like a relic with its own powers. Relics in HtV invoke Warehouse 13 style games. Mummy tombs and relics is a given. <br /> <br /> For the most part, magic items make sense in most of those games. In Beast, there's no story or legend about primordial monsters using magic items. Their power is the power of the elements, of the fear and chaos. Magic items tend to be seen as the symbol of civilization and humanity. Its just not thematically appropriate here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also.. I cant recall what the beast aura/blood effects was supposed to be for crossover purposes. </div> </div> </div> Depends on what you mean. Vampires have their Predator's Aura, werewolves their Aspects, and magi their Nimbus. Meanwhile, demons have no aura effect, I haven't heard anything about Prometheans or Changelings getting an aura either. Its possible the big three are the only ones getting an aura that can be used as a weapon. <br /> <br /> If you mean the effect of vampires drinking Beast blood, and what auras look like? Neither exist in 2e. Auras don't use visual cues like 1e did, and vampires don't suffer from drinking supernatural blood anymore (barring ST calls, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:17:47-08:00","id":758674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions#post757625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed there was a distinct lack of items that beast can craft that are specific to their splat... did I miss something or is that intentional? (can they use the gear of other supers?)<br /> <br /> Also.. I cant recall what the beast aura/blood effects was supposed to be for crossover purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Probably intentional, but a case could be made for items made from pure dreamstuff, although nothing in the book prevents physical items from transubstantiating. Family Ties could work for Item Activation, although items with fuel costs would be tough. Don't see it working with Gadgets, though, for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> 2. The Beast's Aura effect (Passing Resemblance) is designed to keep them from getting killed on sight. It's more about projecting trustworthiness than anything else. As to their blood, Taste for the Strange allows you to treat Beast blood as Kindred Vitae for feeding purposes but that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 11-06-2015, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T15:05:53-08:00","id":759405,"title":"","content":"A beast would have no problem finding magic items, if they were so inclined- relics, awakened items, ghost fetishes, cursed items, trinkets.<br /> <br /> If I were to add item crafting, my first response would be to give them access to a new lair trait, or perhaps a merit -cornerstones.<br /> <br /> Cornerstones manifest as items that can be removed from the beast's lair, they are essentially an additional manifestation of the beast's lair. The beast always knows where it is by just thinking about it. <br /> <br /> In the beast's possession, it acts as an imposed lair trait.<br /> <br /> In the possession of someone else, a beast can use it as a conduit to travel to it, like a lair, but only if the item is activated in some way- a ring turned, a sword unsheathed or fed blood, a cup drunk from, etc.<br /> <br /> Having it in someone else's possession is a two edged sword though, anyone with the cornerstone can use it enter the beast's lair. <br /> <br /> Additionally, cornerstones are capable of manifesting lair traits- a sword might glow with blinding light, or burn with the burning trait. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:27:06-08:00","id":759489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions?p=759405#post759405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A beast would have no problem finding magic items, if they were so inclined- relics, awakened items, ghost fetishes, cursed items, trinkets.<br /> <br /> If I were to add item crafting, my first response would be to give them access to a new lair trait, or perhaps a merit -cornerstones.<br /> <br /> Cornerstones manifest as items that can be removed from the beast's lair, they are essentially an additional manifestation of the beast's lair. The beast always knows where it is by just thinking about it.<br /> <br /> In the beast's possession, it acts as an imposed lair trait.<br /> <br /> In the possession of someone else, a beast can use it as a conduit to travel to it, like a lair, but only if the item is activated in some way- a ring turned, a sword unsheathed or fed blood, a cup drunk from, etc.<br /> <br /> Having it in someone else's possession is a two edged sword though, anyone with the cornerstone can use it enter the beast's lair.<br /> <br /> Additionally, cornerstones are capable of manifesting lair traits- a sword might glow with blinding light, or burn with the burning trait.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I like your Cornerstones idea, but the name needs more oomph. Something that plays with the notion they are extensions of the Lair. They could be called Protrusions. I think that has the right connotation of unpleasantness. It brings to mind things like bony spikes, oozing tumors, tree branches like skeleton hands, and other horrid growths with an Atavism flavor.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:16:55-08:00","id":759599,"title":"","content":"Matt said, long before the Kickstarter, that <b>Beast</b> items might show up in the <b>Players' Guide</b> supplement. Key word is <i>might</i>, and I probably wouldn't count on it anyway; it doesn't seem necessary, though it might be interesting to see what someone could come up with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T21:24:33-08:00","id":759701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions?p=757754#post757754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one of the Kindred gets anything special for drinking their blood. If I remember correctly, 1e had some specific rules for what each splat's blood meant in terms of Vitae for a Kindred. Promethean blood was stale and gave half Vitae, Uratha blood was especially nourishing and gave a penalty to resist Frenzy, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>In second edition, supernatural blood is the same as human blood for Kindred purposes, barring anything that says otherwise further down the road. Unless you have Unnatural Affinity, in which case certain kinds can stand in for vampire blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T23:38:10-08:00","id":759778,"title":"","content":"I thought of two other ideas for beast magic items, not as complete rules wise as my first idea, but perhaps the ideas will inspire someone.<br /> <br /> 1) Trophies- Perhaps they can store satiety for later, or possessing a trophy makes using nightmares easier on subjects that are symbolically linked to the trophy. <br /> <br /> 2) Wards/aegis/<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">gorgoneia- The beast can channel fear into objects as protective amulets. Scare intruders away from a building, scare away attackers in battle, perhaps even scaring away misfortune or disease if you want to go that far. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T02:29:37-08:00","id":759840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions?p=759778#post759778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .<br /> 1) Trophies- Perhaps they can store satiety for later, or possessing a trophy makes using nightmares easier on subjects that are symbolically linked to the trophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Trophies&quot; strike me as more of a Hero thing. The head of Medusa, the poisonous blood of the Hydra . . . things taken from a slain Beast's corpse, and made to serve the Hero's purposes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:19:36-08:00","id":759856,"title":"","content":"Beasts can take stuff from the astral. Want a magic sword? How does Excalibur sound? You just need to find the astral version of King Arthur and nick it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:46:56-08:00","id":760286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions?p=759856#post759856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts can take stuff from the astral. Want a magic sword? How does Excalibur sound? You just need to find the astral version of King Arthur and nick it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Correction: A version of Excalibur. The Astral includes every version of camelot, king arthur, and excalibur ever imagined in human history. <br /> <br /> There are already rules for that, pretty much, chimerical items from Astral Realms. <br /> <br /> They can also come to earth by inspiring people to remake them. So in the world of darkness someone might have a dream and recreate mjolnir, or excalibur, or whatever. <br /> <br /> While it would make perfect sense to include chimerical items in a beast game, in the hands of a beast or a hero, it's not really a beast only thing, since like relics even muggles can have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T09:07:53-08:00","id":760694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions?p=759489#post759489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I like your Cornerstones idea, but the name needs more oomph. Something that plays with the notion they are extensions of the Lair. They could be called Protrusions. I think that has the right connotation of unpleasantness. It brings to mind things like bony spikes, oozing tumors, tree branches like skeleton hands, and other horrid growths with an Atavism flavor.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm .. Chimeric Item? Phantasmagoria?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:12:32-08:00","id":760884,"title":"","content":"Chimeric items sounds far too much like chimerical items, which are already a thing in mage, so I wouldn't suggest that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T15:24:47-08:00","id":760975,"title":"","content":"A general merit idea:<b> Astral Panoply</b>. A style merit that lets you form weapons, armor, even a small army of dream-constructs to give you better dream combat stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:02:58-08:00","id":761449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions?p=759840#post759840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Trophies&quot; strike me as more of a Hero thing. The head of Medusa, the poisonous blood of the Hydra . . . things taken from a slain Beast's corpse, and made to serve the Hero's purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be okay with this should it show up in a supplement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Perhaps it can mingle with Anathemas somehow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T19:32:14-08:00","id":761942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions?p=759856#post759856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts can take stuff from the astral. Want a magic sword? How does Excalibur sound? You just need to find the astral version of King Arthur and nick it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a train wreck waiting to happen. Boys and girls, Excalibur was<i> dangerous</i>. We're not talking about some generic +1 trinket. Forged of the old magic, Excalibur was the magical equivalent of having (nuclear) first strike capability. Even knowing the danger, King Arthur himself nearly fell under the sword's sway.<br /> <br /> Bringing Excalibur back to Earth, when every eight year old with a library card knows its name, and wars would start just over the bragging rights . . . And that's before factoring in the sword's <i>own</i> magic. You don't let kids play with fire. Why leave sweating dynamite <i>right there</i>, where anyone could find it? Don't court disaster - leave Excalibur with the Lady of the Lake<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i> I see where you're trying to go, <b>Elfive</b>, and it seems like it could work. Its just Excalibur is . . . overkill, if you only need <i>a</i> magic sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 11-09-2015, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T19:48:47-08:00","id":761951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/757625-no-beast-specific-crafted-items-and-other-odd-questions?p=761942#post761942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like a train wreck waiting to happen. Boys and girls, Excalibur was<i> dangerous</i>. We're not talking about some generic +1 trinket. Forged of the old magic, Excalibur was the magical equivalent of having (nuclear) first strike capability. Even knowing the danger, King Arthur himself nearly fell under the sword's sway.<br /> <br /> Bringing the sword back to Earth, when every eight year old with a library card has heard of the sword, and wars would start just over the bragging rights . . . And that's before factoring in the sword's <i>own</i> magic. You don't let kids play with fire. Why leave sweating dynamite <i>right there</i>, where anyone could find it? Don't court disaster - leave Excalibur with the Lady of the Lake</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely something entering the realm of &quot;The Cult of Celebrity...&quot; Plucking items of legend, out of the whims of Fate, is something that, without an egregiously tacked on system, should solely be the provenance of a(n) (arch)mage. Now, creating a short-lived, narratively similar illusion of a legendary item is not hard to justify, nor would hunting down and binding the spiritual representation of such an item in order to access a measure of that power (were the Supernatural creature doing so a Werewolf, or a medium of similar talents.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T15:25:43-08:00","id":764439,"title":"","content":"Chimerical items, which is what Excalibur and other such objects out of the astral are, use the artifact rules from Mage, except non mages can use them.<br /> <br /> As for chimerical items that would deserve a rating of N/A instead of 1 through 5, well the origin of such an item really has no bearing on anything. <br /> <br /> If you wouldn't let your players have a fetish, trinket, artifact, etc of N/A, there's no reason to let them have a chimerical item of N/A value either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}